To be honest, I don't see a big problem with #1. We don't usually claim=20
that everything in the same selma'o has the same scoping implications --=20
think about KOhA. And we can't even claim it for terms -- {ca da} is a=20
scoping term while {lo broda} is not. (Please correct me if I am abusing=20
the term "term".)

#2 seems awkward because {soi} would then be redundant, so what's the=20
point. #3 seems awkward because I'm not sure how this new grammatical=20
category would look, but it seems like it'd be quite similar to a term, so=
=20
it would "infect" a lot of grammar rules.

#4 would work too, I think.

- mu'o mi'e durkavore

